# Copy to `.env` for local tooling, or set these in Railway (Variables tab).

# --- PostgreSQL (Railway Postgres injects this on the API service)
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE

# Local dev without DATABASE_URL: use `ConnectionStrings:Database` in
# `backend/appsettings.Development.json` or `dotnet user-secrets` (see comments below).

# --- API (.NET): CORS (browser calls from your SPA origin)
# Production example:
# ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://gezify.app
# ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://your-frontend.up.railway.app

# --- API: JWT signing (HS256, minimum 32 characters)
# Prefer a long random string in production.
# JWT_SECRET=...
# Alternative names (any one):
# AUTH_JWT_SECRET=...
# Or nested: Auth__Jwt__SecretKey=...  (maps to Auth:Jwt:SecretKey)

# --- API: Google OAuth (Authorization Code flow; server exchanges code for tokens)
# Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application) in Google Cloud Console.
# Application type: Web; Authorized redirect URI must match the SPA, e.g.:
#   https://gezify.app/auth/callback
# (Use your preview/staging URL when not in production.)
# Scopes used by the app: openid, email, profile
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# Or nested: Auth__Google__ClientId / Auth__Google__ClientSecret

# --- API: ExchangeRate-API (server-side only)
# EXCHANGE_RATE_API_KEY=...

# --- API: SendGrid (server-side only)
# SENDGRID_API_KEY=...

# --- API: Invitation links (base URL for emails) and signing
# INVITATION_BASE_URL=https://gezify.app
# INVITATION_SIGNING_KEY=...   # long random secret; must match across deploys

# --- Local development quick start (backend folder)
#   dotnet user-secrets init
#   dotnet user-secrets set "ConnectionStrings:Database" "Host=localhost;Port=5432;Database=gezify;Username=postgres;Password=YOUR_PASSWORD"
#   dotnet user-secrets set "Auth:Google:ClientId" "..."
#   dotnet user-secrets set "Auth:Google:ClientSecret" "..."
#   dotnet user-secrets set "Auth:Jwt:SecretKey" "your-long-random-secret-at-least-32-chars"

# --- Production database migrations (§11.3)
# Not applied on Railway container start. Use GitHub Actions (see .github/workflows/database-migrate.yml):
#   Add repo secret DATABASE_URL (same as Railway Postgres).
# Or from your machine:
#   dotnet tool restore
#   cd backend && dotnet ef database update --project Gezify.Api.csproj --startup-project Gezify.Api.csproj
#   (set DATABASE_URL or ConnectionStrings:Database; use ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production for managed SSL)
